# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, in the index AND in the working tree.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set locally and this repository carried no
# `.gitattributes`, so every text file was rewritten to CRLF in the working
# tree on checkout. That is harmless for almost everything here: DC-1
# normalises CRLF to LF before hashing, so every digest, seal, registry row and
# approval binding is immune to it by construction.
#
# It is NOT harmless in two places.
#
# 1. A generated artifact compared byte-for-byte.
#    `params/generated/SEWCP-200.csv` is emitted with LF endings and no
#    byte-order mark and is imported directly by Fusion 360 at CAD package step
#    6.02. A stash/checkout round-trip rewrote it to CRLF and broke
#    `python -m aief_params check`, which is how this file first came to exist.
#
# 2. Check V-25, which reads the WORKING TREE and not the index: "Every text
#    artifact under .ai/ and every artifact registered in project/FROZEN.md ...
#    uses LF line endings exclusively". A checkout under `core.autocrlf=true`
#    therefore breaks V-25 by construction, and V-25 is an AMD-31 compile-time
#    precondition of Compiler Stage 6. This is exactly the exposure recorded at
#    OI-V-05 FIND-Q3-4 ("a future checkout may rewrite working-tree files to
#    CRLF and break the literal V-25 working-tree condition; a `.gitattributes`
#    declaring LF for `.ai/**` is a `repository-engineer` action"), and it was
#    realised: 62 files carried CR at the start of session S-2026-08-11-06.
#
# WHY ONE BLANKET RULE RATHER THAN A LIST OF PARTITIONS. The first repair here
# declared `.ai/**`, `spec/**`, `framework/**` and `*.py` - the V-25 domain plus
# the tooling. That left `cad/**`, `releases/**`, `implementation/**` and
# `ENGINEERING.md` under autocrlf, and 48 tracked files were still CRLF in the
# working tree immediately after the repair. Enumerating partitions means the
# next partition is missed the same way.
#
# The blanket rule was safe when written because it was checked rather than
# assumed: EVERY tracked file in this repository decoded as UTF-8 and contained
# no NUL octet - 232 `.md`, 91 `.py`, 79 `.gitkeep`, 69 `.json`, one `.csv`,
# one `.manifest`, and four extensionless text artifacts (`.ai/core/VERSION`,
# `.ai/core/validation/MANIFEST`, `.ai/project/ledger/HEAD`, `LICENSE`). There
# was no binary content to damage. Re-run that check before adding any.
#
# THAT CHECK WAS RE-RUN, AND BINARY CONTENT WAS THEN ADDED. `ECR-D-015`
# (session `S-2026-08-17-01`) mirrors the 61 CAD deliverables into the tree at
# the paths `SEDEP-PMP-002` §3.1 declares. Of the 61: **14 PDF and 10 STL carry
# NUL octets and do not decode as UTF-8**, and the other 37 - STEP, SVG,
# provenance JSON, BOM CSV - are UTF-8 but carry CRLF. Under `* text eol=lf`
# git would corrupt the 24 binaries outright and rewrite the 37 to LF, moving
# every one of the 61 digests `cad/DELIVERABLES.md` registers and that
# `releases/RELEASE_READINESS_S-2026-08-11-06.md` §5 verified bi-directionally.
#
# So the deliverable subtrees are declared `-text`: octets in, octets out,
# no normalisation in either direction. They are GENERATED EVIDENCE BOUND BY
# DIGEST, not source - the byte identity IS the record, and a line-ending
# policy has no business touching it. Scoped by path, never by extension, so
# the `.json` and `.csv` files elsewhere in the tree stay under the blanket
# rule where they belong. The `V-25` domain is untouched - no deliverable is
# under `.ai/` and none is registered in `project/FROZEN.md`.
#
# THE CENSUS ABOVE IS A MEASUREMENT AND IT GOES STALE. An independent audit
# found the paragraph above citing "69 `.json`" against 70 observed - already
# wrong at the parent commit, because a count written into a comment is not
# recomputed by anything. Today: 81 `.json`, 2 `.csv`, 257 `.md`, 103 `.py`,
# 75 `.gitkeep`. Do not trust these either; recompute with `git ls-files`.
# What is NOT a stale count, and is the operative property, is checked by the
# `validate` workflow on every push: no CR in the `V-25` domain after a clean
# checkout, and every binary deliverable still carrying its NUL octets.
#
# `text` is stated explicitly rather than left to `text=auto` heuristics, so
# the outcome does not depend on git's content sniffing.
#
# No registered digest moves under any of this: DC-1 normalises CRLF to LF
# before hashing, so it is a working-tree and index-normalisation repair only.
# Verified by comparing the DC-1 of every affected file before and after.

* text eol=lf

# Kept explicit for the two cases whose reasons are recorded above, so that
# deleting the blanket rule does not silently un-fix them.
params/generated/*.csv text eol=lf
.gitattributes         text eol=lf

# CAD deliverables - ECR-D-015. Byte-preserved, never normalised. Ordered
# after the blanket rule because the last matching line wins.
cad/exports/**       -text
cad/bom/**           -text
drawings/parts/**    -text
drawings/assembly/** -text
# The remaining declared drawing directories of SEDEP-PMP-002 s1. They hold
# only .gitkeep today, so nothing is protected by adding them - which is the
# point: an independent audit observed that the trap this file's own comment
# warns about was re-armed for exactly these four, because the -text scoping
# named the two subtrees that happened to have content rather than the class
# of directory that holds drawings. `drawings/defs/**` is deliberately NOT
# here: it is MIT-licensed Python source and belongs under the blanket rule.
drawings/icd/**       -text
drawings/templates/** -text
drawings/redlines/**  -text
